/-!
# The reduction of a general formal algebraic space

Let `S` be a scheme contained in a big fppf site `B` and let `X` be a formal algebraic space
over `S`. **Stacks 0AIN** asserts that `X` has a reduction: a reduced algebraic space `X_red`
together with a representable morphism `X_red ⟶ X` which is a thickening and through which
every morphism to `X` from a reduced algebraic space factors uniquely. The affine case is
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.exists_isReduction_of_isAffineFormalAlgebraicSpace`; this file
proves the general case.

## The construction

Let `{X_i ⟶ X}` be an atlas of `X` by affine formal algebraic spaces. Each `X_i` has a
reduction, carried by a reduced *affine* object `T_i` of the site
(`…exists_isReduction_reduced_affine_siteObject_of_isAffineFormal`). The candidate reduction is
the subsheaf
`X_red = (⋃ᵢ image(h_{T_i} ⟶ X))^#`
of `X` generated by their images. Three things have to be checked, and they are exactly the
three fields the library's criterion
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isReduction_of_isRepresentableThickening` asks for.

*The inclusion is a representable thickening.* The base change of `X_red ⟶ X` along `X_i ⟶ X`
is the reduction of `X_i`, because a section of `X_i` landing in the image of some `h_{T_j}`
already lands in the image of `h_{T_i}`: the overlap is reduced and factors uniquely through
the reduction of `X_i` by its universal property. The claim then follows by descent, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isRepresentableThickening_of_isPullback_etale_cover`.

*It is an algebraic space.* That is
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isAlgebraicSpaceULift_of_reduced_etale_cover_of_mono_sheafHom`,
applied to the same cartesian squares.

*It is reduced.* Every étale chart of `X_red` is reduced: a point of the chart lands, locally,
in the image of one `h_{T_i}`, and the fibre of the chart over a reduced object of the site is
reduced, so the chart's own reduced closed subscheme is all of it.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.exists_isReduction_of_isFormalAlgebraicSpace`: **Stacks
  0AIN** in general.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.nonempty_reduction_of_isFormalAlgebraicSpace` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.reduction`: the reduction in the bundled shape
  `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.Reduction` that the étale sites of Stacks 0DEA and their
  functoriality consume, which needs in addition that the reduction's presheaf take values in
  the value universe of the site — automatic, by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_comp_uliftFunctor_iso_of_isAlgebraicSpaceULift`.

## Implementation notes

The subsheaf is formed as `CategoryTheory.Subfunctor.sheafify` of the supremum of the ranges,
so its inclusion is a monomorphism by construction and no separate argument is needed for that.
Identifying its base change along `X_i` with the reduction of `X_i` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isPullback_of_preimage_eq_range` fed by
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.preimage_sheafify_iSup_range_eq_range`, whose hypothesis is the
overlap statement `…exists_lift_reduced_chart_overlap`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AIN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AIN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AIM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AIM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DEA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DEA)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace

universe u

/-! ### Two cartesian-square manipulations -/

/-- Two sections of a cartesian square whose other leg is a monomorphism agree. -/
private theorem hom_ext_of_isPullback_snd_mono {C : Type*} [Category C] {A F T X : C}
    {a : A ⟶ F} {q : A ⟶ T} {i : F ⟶ X} {f : T ⟶ X} (h : IsPullback a q i f) [Mono q]
    (g₁ g₂ : T ⟶ F) (h₁ : g₁ ≫ i = f) (h₂ : g₂ ≫ i = f) : g₁ = g₂ := by
  have hw₁ : g₁ ≫ i = 𝟙 T ≫ f := h₁.trans (Category.id_comp f).symm
  have hw₂ : g₂ ≫ i = 𝟙 T ≫ f := h₂.trans (Category.id_comp f).symm
  have he : h.lift g₁ (𝟙 T) hw₁ = h.lift g₂ (𝟙 T) hw₂ :=
    (cancel_mono q).1 (by rw [h.lift_snd, h.lift_snd])
  simpa using congrArg (· ≫ a) he

/-- A section lifting uniquely along a cartesian square whose other leg is an isomorphism. -/
private theorem existsUnique_lift_of_isPullback_snd_isIso {C : Type*} [Category C] {A F T X : C}
    {a : A ⟶ F} {q : A ⟶ T} {i : F ⟶ X} {f : T ⟶ X} (h : IsPullback a q i f) [IsIso q] :
    ∃! g : T ⟶ F, g ≫ i = f := by
  have hg : (inv q ≫ a) ≫ i = f := by rw [Category.assoc, h.w, IsIso.inv_hom_id_assoc]
  exact ⟨_, hg, fun g hg' ↦ hom_ext_of_isPullback_snd_mono h _ _ hg' hg⟩

/-- **A cartesian square whose upper left corner factors through a monomorphism into its upper
right corner is cartesian for that monomorphism composed into the lower leg.** -/
private theorem isPullback_of_factorization_through_mono {C : Type*} [Category C]
    {P U V W X : C} {a : P ⟶ U} {b : P ⟶ V} {f : U ⟶ X} {g : V ⟶ X}
    (h : IsPullback a b f g) (jj : W ⟶ U) [Mono jj] (kk : P ⟶ W) (hk : kk ≫ jj = a) :
    IsPullback kk b (jj ≫ f) g := by
  apply IsPullback.mk'
  · rw [← Category.assoc, hk, h.w]
  · intro T q r h₁ h₂
    apply h.hom_ext _ h₂
    rw [← hk, ← Category.assoc, h₁, Category.assoc]
  · intro T q r hqr
    have hw : (q ≫ jj) ≫ f = r ≫ g := by simpa only [Category.assoc] using hqr
    refine ⟨h.lift (q ≫ jj) r hw, ?_, h.lift_snd _ _ _⟩
    apply (cancel_mono jj).1
    rw [Category.assoc, hk, h.lift_fst]

/-! ### The preimage of a sheafified union of ranges -/

/-- A section of a union of ranges of morphisms lies in the range of one of them. -/
private theorem exists_eq_of_mem_iSup_range.{w} {C : Type*} [Category C]
    {F : C ⥤ Type w} {I : Type*} {P : I → C ⥤ Type w} (a : ∀ i, P i ⟶ F) {V : C} {x : F.obj V}
    (hx : x ∈ (⨆ i, Subfunctor.range (a i)).obj V) : ∃ i y, (a i).app V y = x := by
  simpa only [Subfunctor.iSup_obj, Set.mem_iUnion, Subfunctor.range_obj, Set.mem_range] using hx

/-- **A sheafified union of ranges pulls back to one of them.** Let `r i : Z i ⟶ Y i` be
monomorphisms of sheaves and `f i : Y i ⟶ X` arbitrary. If a section of `Y j` whose image in
`X` lies in the image of some `Z i` already lies in the image of `Z j`, then the preimage under
`f j` of the sheafification of `⋃ᵢ image(Z i ⟶ X)` is exactly the image of `Z j`. -/
theorem preimage_sheafify_iSup_range_eq_range {C : Type*} [Category C]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) {I : Type*} {X : Sheaf J (Type u)}
    {Y Z : I → Sheaf J (Type u)} (f : ∀ i, Y i ⟶ X) (r : ∀ i, Z i ⟶ Y i) [∀ i, Mono (r i)]
    (hsat : ∀ i j (T : Cᵒᵖ) (a : (Z i).obj.obj T) (b : (Y j).obj.obj T),
      ((r i ≫ f i).hom.app T) a = (f j).hom.app T b →
        b ∈ (Subfunctor.range (r j).hom).obj T)
    (j : I) :
    ((⨆ i, Subfunctor.range (r i ≫ f i).hom).sheafify J).preimage (f j).hom =
      Subfunctor.range (r j).hom := by
  let A : Subfunctor X.obj := ⨆ i, Subfunctor.range (r i ≫ f i).hom
  have hrmono : Mono (r j).hom := (sheafToPresheaf J (Type u)).map_mono (r j)
  have hR : Presieve.IsSheaf J (Subfunctor.range (r j).hom).toFunctor :=
    (isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J _).1
      ((Presheaf.isSheaf_of_iso_iff (asIso (Subfunctor.toRange (r j).hom))).1 (Z j).property)
  ext T b
  constructor
  · intro hb
    apply ((Subfunctor.range (r j).hom).isSheaf_iff
      ((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type J _).1 (Y j).property)).1 hR T b
    change A.sieveOfSection ((f j).hom.app T b) ∈ J T.unop at hb
    apply J.superset_covering ?_ hb
    intro V g hg
    obtain ⟨i, a, ha⟩ := exists_eq_of_mem_iSup_range (fun i ↦ (r i ≫ f i).hom) hg
    exact hsat i j (Opposite.op V) a ((Y j).obj.map g.op b) <|
      ha.trans ((f j).hom.naturality_apply g.op b).symm
  · rintro ⟨a, rfl⟩
    apply A.le_sheafify J
    show ((r j ≫ f j).hom.app T) a ∈ A.obj T
    exact (le_iSup (fun i ↦ Subfunctor.range (r i ≫ f i).hom) j) T ⟨a, rfl⟩

/-- **A subfunctor whose preimage along a morphism is the range of a monomorphism is pulled back
to it.** -/
theorem isPullback_of_preimage_eq_range {C : Type*} [Category C] {F U V : C ⥤ Type u}
    (G : Subfunctor F) (r : U ⟶ V) [Mono r] (f : V ⟶ F) (kk : U ⟶ G.toFunctor)
    (hk : kk ≫ G.ι = r ≫ f) (heq : G.preimage f = Subfunctor.range r) :
    IsPullback kk r G.ι f := by
  apply IsPullback.mk' hk
  · intro T a b _ h
    exact (cancel_mono r).1 h
  · intro T a b hab
    have hb : Subfunctor.range b ≤ Subfunctor.range r := by
      rw [← heq]
      intro V' x hx
      obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := hx
      have h := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (congr_app hab V') t
      change (a.app V' t).val = (f.app V') (b.app V' t) at h
      show (f.app V') (b.app V' t) ∈ G.obj V'
      rw [← h]
      exact (a.app V' t).property
    let l := Subfunctor.lift b hb ≫ inv (Subfunctor.toRange r)
    have hl : l ≫ r = b := by
      have hi : inv (Subfunctor.toRange r) ≫ r = (Subfunctor.range r).ι :=
        (IsIso.inv_comp_eq _).2 (Subfunctor.toRange_ι r).symm
      simp only [l, Category.assoc, hi, Subfunctor.lift_ι]
    refine ⟨l, ?_, hl⟩
    apply (cancel_mono G.ι).1
    rw [Category.assoc, hk, ← Category.assoc, hl, hab]

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-! ### A representable thickening of fppf sheaves is a monomorphism -/

/-- **A representable thickening of fppf sheaves is a monomorphism.** It is one on the
underlying presheaves, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.mono_of_isRepresentableThickeningULift`, and the inclusion of
sheaves into presheaves reflects monomorphisms. -/
theorem mono_of_isRepresentableThickening {F X : FppfSheaf B S hS} (i : F ⟶ X)
    (hi : Space.IsRepresentableThickeningULift.{u + 1} B S hS i.hom) : Mono i :=
  (sheafToPresheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Type (u + 1))).mono_of_mono_map
    (mono_of_isRepresentableThickeningULift B S hS hi)

/-! ### Reducedness of an étale chart of the glued reduction -/

/-- **A point of an étale chart which maps into a reduced object of the site lifts to the
chart's reduced closed subscheme.** The fibre of the chart over the reduced object is reduced,
being étale over it, so it lifts along the chart's own reduced closed subscheme, and the point
is carried along. -/
theorem exists_lift_siteReductionMap_of_relative_etale
    {R : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (u + 1)} (T V : BigFppfOver B S hS)
    (hV : IsReduced ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V))
    (p : (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).obj T ⟶ R)
    (hp : (MorphismProperty.inverseImage (@Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).relative (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}) p)
    (kk : (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).obj V ⟶ R) (U : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : ((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).obj T).obj U) (y : ((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).obj V).obj U)
    (hxy : p.app U x = kk.app U y) :
    ∃ z, ((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map (siteReductionMap B S hS T)).app U z = x := by
  let Hs := BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS
  let r := siteReductionMap B S hS T
  have _ : Etale (Hs.map (hp.rep.snd kk)) := hp.property_snd kk
  have _ : IsReduced (Hs.obj V) := hV
  have hW : IsReduced (Hs.obj (hp.rep.pullback kk)) :=
    isReduced_of_smooth (Hs.map (hp.rep.snd kk))
  let b : hp.rep.pullback kk ⟶ T := (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).preimage (hp.rep.fst kk)
  have hb : (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map b = hp.rep.fst kk :=
    (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map_preimage _
  obtain ⟨l, hl⟩ := exists_lift_siteReduction_of_isReduced B S hS r
    (isThickening_toScheme_map_siteReductionMap B S hS T) hW b
  have hpb := (hp.rep.isPullback kk).map
    ((evaluation (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ (Type (u + 1))).obj U)
  obtain ⟨z, hz, -⟩ := Types.exists_of_isPullback hpb x y hxy
  refine ⟨((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map l).app U z, ?_⟩
  have hmap : (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map l ≫ (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map r = hp.rep.fst kk := by
    rw [← Functor.map_comp, hl, hb]
  show (((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map l ≫ (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map r).app U) z = x
  rw [hmap]
  exact hz

/-- **Every étale chart of a sheafified union of images of reduced objects of the site is
reduced.** Each point of the chart lands locally in the image of one member, and the fibre of
the chart over that reduced member is reduced, so the chart's reduced closed subscheme is
locally surjective onto it. -/
theorem isReduced_of_relative_etale_into_sheafify_iSup_range {I : Type (u + 1)}
    (X : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (u + 1)) (Ti : I → BigFppfOver B S hS)
    (hTi : ∀ i, IsReduced ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (Ti i)))
    (a : ∀ i, (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).obj (Ti i) ⟶ X) (T : BigFppfOver B S hS)
    (p : (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).obj T ⟶
      ((⨆ i, Subfunctor.range (a i)).sheafify (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS)).toFunctor)
    (hp : (MorphismProperty.inverseImage (@Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).relative (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}) p) :
    IsReduced ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T) := by
  let J := BigFppfOver.topology B S hS
  let A : Subfunctor X := ⨆ i, Subfunctor.range (a i)
  let kk (i : I) : (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).obj (Ti i) ⟶ (A.sheafify J).toFunctor :=
    Subfunctor.lift (a i)
      ((le_iSup (fun i ↦ Subfunctor.range (a i)) i).trans (A.le_sheafify J))
  apply isReduced_of_isLocallySurjective_siteReductionMap B S hS T
  refine ⟨fun {U} x ↦ ?_⟩
  have hx : A.sieveOfSection (p.app (Opposite.op U) x).val ∈ J U :=
    (p.app (Opposite.op U) x).property
  refine J.superset_covering (fun V g hg ↦ ?_) hx
  obtain ⟨i, y, hy⟩ := exists_eq_of_mem_iSup_range a hg
  have hw : p.app (Opposite.op V) (((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).obj T).map g.op x) =
      (kk i).app (Opposite.op V) y :=
    Subtype.ext <| (congrArg Subtype.val (p.naturality_apply g.op x)).trans hy.symm
  exact exists_lift_siteReductionMap_of_relative_etale B S hS T (Ti i) (hTi i) p hp (kk i)
    (Opposite.op V) (((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).obj T).map g.op x) y hw

/-! ### The overlap statement -/

/-! ### Stacks 0AIN in general -/

/-! ### The reduction in the shape the étale sites consume -/

/-- **Stacks 0AIN for a general formal algebraic space, as a construction.** The chosen
reduction of a formal algebraic space over `S`, in the bundled shape the étale sites of
Stacks 0DEA consume. -/
@[stacks 0AIN "general formal algebraic spaces, as a chosen datum"]
noncomputable def reduction (X : FppfSheaf B S hS) (hX : IsFormalAlgebraicSpace B S hS X) :
    Reduction B S hS X :=
  Classical.choice (nonempty_reduction_of_isFormalAlgebraicSpace hX)

